Check extensional proofs in Eqlog context models

Allow dependent relation signatures to refer to members of earlier model
arguments, so ambient rules can relate distinct context models without
flattening their members. Preserve owner bindings in native and dynamic
evaluators, including foreign members of model relations.

Add examples/ett with a small Lean-like frontend and an Eqlog kernel for
context extension, partial substitutions, identity types with equality
reflection, and finite sums with dependent recursion. Morphisms follow
substitution. Fresh statement scopes keep equality local;
open definitions do not allocate images of hidden body operands.

Allocate three constructor expansion steps per elaborated literal
occurrence and check the module with one close call. Include addition
and induction proofs, and integration coverage for rejected proofs,
context isolation, partial images, and the computation bound.
